(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2608201100-kotoba-lang-process-and-fs-host-planes")
  (:adr/title "kotoba-lang/process and fs host planes")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-20")
  (:adr/body "# kotoba-lang/process + fs host planes\n\n## Status\naccepted (2026-08-20)\n\n## Context\nApps (cloud-itonami-app and others) still used ambient ProcessBuilder and\njava.nio. kotoba-lang/fs already provided IFilesystem + fs-host jail.\nprocess/spawn existed as catalog wire id 20 and provider.process, but there\nwas no foundational stdlib twin of fs, and no capability-process-spawn package\n(only capability-process-list).\n\n## Decision\n1. Land kotoba-lang/process: pure validate-spawn + IProcess + process-host\n   (clj ProcessBuilder / cljs spawnSync). No ambient PATH; :binaries map only.\n2. Land kotoba-lang/capability-process-spawn (contract-only) for process/spawn.\n3. Register both in west (extra-projects + pins).\n4. Apps inject handles via a host namespace; do not call ProcessBuilder/Files\n   from product code once cut over.\n\n## Consequences\nmax-argv is 64 (docker create lines). Definition CID on the capability package\nis provisional content-addressed identity until content-addressed registration\npipeline hashes the sealed definition. provider.process remains the KIR kit;\nprocess is the zero-kir stdlib apps may depend on directly.\n")))
